  "note": "Annual election of six urban councillors, January 1927. Six seats were filled: four expiries — Henry Hayes, Henry M'Cavana, William Nabney and Thomas J. Patterson — and two casual vacancies caused by the disqualification of William Henry Elliott and John K. Lyons. Patterson withdrew from the election, leaving six candidates for the six seats, who were returned unopposed: Clugston, Hunter, Hayes, M'Cavana, Gookin and Nabney (Belfast News-Letter, 7 January 1927, p. 8). Patterson and John Wallace were then co-opted into the two casual vacancies (Provincial Paragraphs, 25 and 29 January 1927). Thomas J. Patterson, a retiring member, withdrew and so prevented a contest for the six vacancies. Returned unopposed."
